        "original_id": "3aa350f0-912b-576f-8794-17254439575b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Centaurium, Dacrydium, Schenkia\n- Taxonomy: Gentianaceae, Chironieae, Chironiinae, Podocarpaceae\n\nFacts:\n- Centaurium, also called centaury, is a genus of 20 species in the gentian family Gentianaceae, tribe Chironieae, subtribe Chironiinae.\n- Dacrydium is a genus of conifers in the podocarp family Podocarpaceae.\n- Dacrydium currently includes sixteen recognized species of evergreen dioecious trees and shrubs.\n- Schenkia is sometimes included in the genus Centaurium.",
